Subject: [PATCH] GS GPU renderer: batch data through one ring buffer; runtime
 threads named

Each batch's vertices, draws, CLUTs and mesh/moment inputs were glBufferData'd fresh: three to
six new buffer stores a batch, 10-20 thousand a second at 60 frames in a level. They now go
through one 128 MB persistently mapped buffer made once, eight segments fenced in turn (the
compute passes that write moment/mesh vertices bind the batch's stretch). PS2X_GPU_RING=0: the
old way. Verified: a level renders as before; the ring never waited for the GPU in Amazon.

The runtime's own threads now carry names (Present, VBlankWatch, Vif1, GsFeed, GsBackend,
TexturePack) for profilers and debuggers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
